        <briefdescription>
<para>Select the optimal execution path for a query. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The planner evaluates paths 1–5 in order from cheapest to most expensive. Any failed gate causes a fall-through to the next path with the appropriate <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacethemis_1_1evaluation_1a142bb8182e534e4057c9b31b464b9008" kindref="member">FallbackReason</ref></computeroutput>. The safe default is Path 4 (DirectExactGraph).</para>
<para>After the decision is made, <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1evaluation_1_1_planner_observer_1a194eef3877c6cefbb2df2e5a78f67135" kindref="member">PlannerObserver::onDecision()</ref></computeroutput> is called (if an observer was registered) with the decision and the wall-clock latency of the planner logic in microseconds.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>Distributed Path 5 is only eligible when distributed mode signals are set; it is not evaluated in the normal 1–4 fallback chain. Callers may request Path 5 explicitly by setting eligibility signals that disable paths 1–3 while marking <computeroutput>distributed_multi_shard</computeroutput>.</para>
</simplesect>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>eligibility</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Runtime hardware and module-readiness signals. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>freshness</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Tensor artifact freshness state. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>config</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Versioned policy thresholds. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>A <ref refid="structthemis_1_1evaluation_1_1_planner_decision" kindref="compound">PlannerDecision</ref> with the selected path and any fallback reason. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
